{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Where a notification takes the app. Every item of GET /api/v1/notifications has a `link`: the web path of what it is about. The apps map it to a screen and the item on it (`kind`, `id`). A tap on a notification in the app's inbox, or on the local notification for a single new item, opens it.",
  "rules": [
    "A link is a path on the company's own server, starting with a single '/'. A full URL, a '//host' link or no link opens the notifications inbox.",
    "IDs must be UUIDs (compared lower-case). A link to a screen with an ID that isn't one opens that screen without an item; /inbox with neither opens the approvals inbox.",
    "Links to screens the apps don't have (documents, people, payroll runs, settings, the outlet roster, the home page) open the notifications inbox, where the item is.",
    "approvalTask opens that task's decision when it still waits for this person; approvalRequest opens the waiting task for that request. Otherwise the approvals inbox says the request no longer waits.",
    "The local notification text never changes (a count only, background-refresh-cases.json). When it announces exactly one new unread item with a link, its tap opens that item and marks the notification read; with several it opens the approvals inbox when any is an approval, otherwise the notifications inbox.",
    "A screen the server has switched off (meta features) opens the notifications inbox instead."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "link": "/inbox?task=0190A0B0-0000-7000-8000-0000000000A1",
      "kind": "approvalTask",
      "id": "0190a0b0-0000-7000-8000-0000000000a1"
    },
    {
      "link": "/inbox?request=0190a0b0-0000-7000-8000-0000000000a2",
